Subject: [PATCH] Fix PDF currency glyph, add voucher-detail column, center
 headers, tidy Rs.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Combines two rounds of ledger-PDF fixes into one commit (the first round's
patch hadn't been applied yet, so folding this in avoids another multi-
patch mixup):

- jsPDF's built-in Helvetica has no ₹ glyph, so it silently substituted
  an unrelated character in front of every figure. Add fmtCurrencyPdf/
  fmtCurrencyPdf2 (PDF-only, "Rs." convention already used by
  generatePriceListPDF.js) and use them everywhere a jsPDF document
  renders currency — the ledger table, the Insights tab's 9 report PDF
  exports, and the Orders tab export.
- Add a "Details" column to the ledger table carrying the same per-
  voucher info the app's own expand view shows (reference, credit-note
  reason, journal accounts) — a static PDF can't have a tap-to-expand,
  so every row prints pre-expanded instead. Switched to landscape to fit
  it and give the money columns room (also fixes them overflowing).
- Table headers are now center-aligned, and "Rs." is stated once in the
  Debit/Credit/Balance headers instead of repeating on every cell — cells
  show plain numbers.

